  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,3).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $2-{s}^{3}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $2s+1$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076578/assets/2fa5c39e68278bdff8ff258f7e2d162956affe67a29119242f53416affee0277.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,3).$",
